==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Crazed Yuki Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Crazed Catgirl Yuki''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
When highly leveled, Crazed Yuki can destroy [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] and [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] enemies efficiently, as her standing range is slightly more than [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] and [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Dragon Cat]]. Due to that, she's able to safely snipe dangerous enemies like [[Le'noir]] and [[Capy]] while meatshields like [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cat]] and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Tank Cat]] take all the hits.

Most importantly, her range allows her to be separated from the standard [[:Category:Anti-dark Cats|anti-dark]] duo of [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] and [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]], as they risk being hit by backliners, unlike her. Keep in mind her damage and health is slightly underwhelming in Normal Form, so only use the other forms.

The largest downside she has throughout all her forms is her attack rate and time of her attacks. Most good anti-dark Ubers have fast attack rates because most dark enemies are fast and have high knockback counts, but Crazed Yuki has a lengthy 16 seconds between attacks. Her attack is also very long and she often gets interupted.

==='''True Form'''===
Crazed Catgirl Yuki gains more health, damage, slow immunity and double movement speed. The stat improvements are very good, the health going up by 47% and the damage going up 25%, enough to make a difference in both of them. The doubled movement speed makes her get to the frontline faster and is just generally good, the Slow Immunity making it so she won't get slowed when getting to the frontline. Sadly, the only relevant enemy the immunity to slow grants her is against [[Professor A.|Professor A]]. Overall, a good [[True Form]] you should consider investing in, considering the [[Catfruit]] cost for it isn't all too high either.

==='''Talents'''===
'''Move Speed Up''' is counterproductive, since despite the blazing fast movement speed it gives her, it actually works to her detriment by turning her even more suicidal.

'''[[Survive|Survive]]''' is fairly useless due to a lack of applicability. Her status as a backliner means that she shouldn't be taking many hits from enemies to begin with, basically only acting as extra assurance in case of emergency. For 235 NP, an ability like this simply isn't worth it.

'''[[Special Abilities#Resist|Resist Wave]]''' is worthless and overly priced.

'''Attack Buff''' is her best Talent since she's a nuker, but remember to upgrade her with [[Catseye]]s first. Yuki also has practically no HP, so '''HP Buff''' doesn't do anything.

==='''Orb'''===
The Massive Damage Orbs against Red/Dark or the Strengthen Orb help her damage by a large margin, and Resist Wave gives her full '''Wave Immunity''', but is not as good as the previous options.

{{Job|Classification = Backliner & Nuker}}

